message.content:
Sure! Below is a minimal example of an “interactive rotating card” that flips when you hover over it.  
Feel free to copy‑paste the code into an `.html` file (or add the CSS to your stylesheet) and tweak the colors, dimensions, or animation speed as you like.

---

### 1️⃣ Markup (HTML)

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card Demo</title>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="styles.css">   <!-- or put the CSS below -->
<style>
/* ------------- CSS goes here ------------- */
</style>
</head>

<body>
<div class="card-wrapper">
    <div class="card">
        <div class="card-face front">
            <h2>Front Side</h2>
            <p>This is the front of the card.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card-face back">
            <h2>Back Side</h2>
            <p>And this is the back!</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
</body>
</html>
```

---

### 2️⃣ Styling (CSS)

```css
/* Basic reset & layout */
body {
    display:flex;
    justify-content:center;
    align-items:center;
    min-height:100vh;
    margin:0;
    background:#f0f0f0;
    font-family:sans-serif;
}

/* Wrapper keeps perspective */
.card-wrapper {
    width:300px;          /* adjust size */
    height:200px;
    perspective:800px;    /* gives depth effect */
}

/* The card itself */
.card {
    width:100%;
    height:100%;
    position:relative;
    transition:transform 0.8s ease-in-out;
    transform-style:preserve-3d;   /* allow children to be positioned in 3D space */
}

/* Flip on hover */
.card:hover {
    transform:rotateY(180deg);     /* change to rotateX(180deg) for vertical flip */
}

/* Common face styles */
.card-face {
    position:absolute;
    width:100%;
    height:100%;
    backface-visibility:hidden;   /* hide backside when flipped */
    border-radius:12px;
    box-shadow:0 4px 8px rgba(0,0,0,.15);
    display:flex;
    flex-direction:column;
    justify-content:center;
    align-items:center;
    padding:20px;
    box-sizing:border-box;
}

/* Front side */
.front {
    background:#fff;
    color:#333;
}

/* Back side – rotated so it's hidden initially */
.back {
    background:#4a90e2;
    color:white;
    transform:rotateY(180deg);      /* same axis as card rotation */
}
```

---

#### How it works

| Step | What happens |
|------|--------------|
| **Wrapper** | `perspective` creates a 3‑D environment. |
| **Card** | `transform-style: preserve-3d` lets its children keep their 3‑D positions. |
| **Faces** | `backface-visibility: hidden` hides the side facing away from the viewer. |
| **Hover** | Rotates the whole card (`rotateY`) while each face is already rotated 180° (so they swap). |

---

### 🎨 Customization Ideas

| Property | Example Change |
|----------|----------------|
| `width / height` | Make the card taller or wider. |
| `background` | Use gradients, images, or solid colors. |
| `transition-duration` | Speed up or slow down the flip. |
| `rotateY` → `rotateX` | Flip vertically instead of horizontally. |
| Add more faces | For a multi‑layered carousel, duplicate `.card-face` blocks with different rotations. |

Enjoy experimenting! If you hit any snags or want extra features (like touch support or 3‑D shadows), just let me know.
